#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44c19ff0-9677-53d2-8b73-50b898324319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357879} {:answer/id #uuid "6774dedc-fdd4-5f55-be9b-b1aa49760ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s+1),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s+1)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357880} {:answer/id #uuid "aeeacb70-038c-551d-b4e6-56d4a72d15d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-1)]⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357881} {:answer/id #uuid "b691cd9a-7c67-541d-8d68-db83364d3b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357882} {:answer/id #uuid "eba30440-2828-585a-aced-8adc91cef4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eba30440-2828-585a-aced-8adc91cef4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357883} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fe88485-d555-5d33-9b5f-a72c01952ade" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5d60c8dc-149c-57b3-9b22-a7e5b2f8c7d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-127727" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{2({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s={e}^{t}-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-1 & =s \\\\ {e}^{t} & =s+1 \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-(s+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
